# Package Boundaries

MintReels owns product/domain logic. PyAI (and other vendors) provide capabilities through adapters.

```text
MintReels Domain → Capability Interface → Provider/Adapter → Vendor
```

## Never import vendors here

`apps/web`, `apps/api`, and `packages/domain` must not import PyAI, AWS SDKs, BullMQ, or FFmpeg.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — in apps/api or packages/domain
import { PyAIClient } from '@mintreels/ai/providers/pyai';

// ✅ GOOD — depend on the interface
import type { SpeechProvider } from '@mintreels/ai';
```

## Apps depend on interfaces

Use `SpeechProvider`, `LLMProvider`, `EmbeddingProvider`, `VectorStoreProvider`, `KnowledgeBaseProvider`, `StorageProvider`, `QueueProvider`. Wire concrete implementations only at composition roots: `apps/api/src/providers/factories.ts` (behind DI tokens in `providers.module.ts`) and `apps/worker/src/providers.ts`. Constructing `QdrantVectorStore` there is allowed — it is the composition root, same as `BullMQQueueProvider`.

## PyAI lives only here

- `packages/ai/src/providers/pyai`
- `packages/knowledge/src/adapters/pyai`

Vendor request/response types stay inside adapters (mappers). Do not leak them into domain types.

## MySQL stores metadata only

Keep `provider` and `provider_knowledge_base_id` (and document provider IDs). Do not store embeddings, vector chunks, or video binaries in MySQL.
